                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Does this imply redundant BMC images will be different? Can't the position be fetched via an EM config?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "README.md",
                    "line": 510,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, there is an include https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/master/meta-phosphor/conf/machine/include/redundant-bmc.inc that's used to enable the redundant-bmc machine feature.  the recipe for this will then key off of that to enable the meson option.  I can put that up now.\n\nOur hardware is such that only the active BMC will have access to either BMC card EEPROM, but we still need to know it on the passive BMC, and also its needed before we choose the role."
                },
                {
                    "file": "README.md",
                    "line": 510,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "It would be great if we pointed that `redundant-bmc` machine specific feature details here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "README.md",
                    "line": 510,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Done."
                }
